n first-person (\"I\") throughout, which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n    39→   - Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` - profile generation needs narrator-aware logic\n    40→   - Fix approach: When a character is identified as the narrator (from plot_summary), build their profile from all first-person statements (\"I thought\", \"I led him\", etc.)\n    41→\n    42→2. **Luchresi missing from character list**\n    43→   - Problem: Luchresi appears 6 times in the text but is not in the character list\n    44→   - Evidence: Pronunciation guide shows Luchresi with 6 occurrences; he's a named character used in dialogue\n    45→   - Impact: -0.5 points on Character Extraction score\n    46→   - Context: He's mentioned as a rival wine expert that Montresor uses to manipulate Fortunato\n    47→   - Location: Likely filtered by mention count threshold or validation logic\n    48→   - Fix approach: Lower threshold OR investigate why a 6-mention character was filtered\n    49→\n    50→3. **`is_narrator` field is false for Montresor**\n    51→   - Problem: `characters[1].is_narrator = false` but plot_summary correctly says \"Montresor, the story's first-person narrator\"\n    52→   - Evidence: Inconsistency between character metadata and plot analysis\n    53→   - Impact: Part of profile score, also data inconsistency\n    54→   - Location: Narrator detection in summary agent vs character metadata\n    55→   - Fix approach: Sync narrator identification from plot_summary back to character metadata\n    56→\n    57→### MEDIUM (Score impact: <0.5 point)\n    58→\n    59→4. **Pronunciation false positives on common words**\n    60→   - Problem: Common English words flagged unnecessarily: jingled, filmy, orbs, leer, familiarly, recoiling, tight-fitting, web-work\n    61→   - Evidence: 56 words flagged total, ~8-10 are common English words\n    62→   - Impact: -0.5 points on Pronunciation score\n    63→   - Location: `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` - word frequency filtering\n    64→   - Fix approach: Add common English word list filter (as noted in ATTEMPT_1_SUMMARY.md)\n    65→\n    66→5. **\"Medoc\" missing from pronunciation guide**\n    67→   - Problem: French wine region \"Medoc\" appears twice in text but not flagged\n    68→   - Evidence: Text has \"draught of the Medoc\" and \"My own fancy grew warm with the Medoc\"\n    69→   - Impact: Minor (-0.1 point)\n    70→   - Location: Pronunciation detection pipeline\n    71→   - Fix approach: Improve foreign word detection\n    72→\n    73→### LOW (Polish items)\n    74→\n    75→6. **Fortunato profile confidence is \"low\"**\n    76→   - Problem: Only character with a profile has low confidence\n    77→   - Evidence: `low_confidence_items: [\"Character: Fortunato\"]`\n    78→   - Impact: Minor quality indicator\n    79→   - Location: Profile generation confidence scoring\n    80→\n    81→## Gap Analysis\n    82→\n    83→Current: 7.70, Target: 8.0, Gap: **0.30 points**\n    84→\n    85→To close the gap, we need approximately:\n    86→- +0.5 on Character Profiles (5→6): Would add +0.15 to overall\n    87→- +0.5 on Character Extraction (7→7.5): Would add +0.125 to overall\n    88→- OR +1 on Pronunciation (7→8): Would add +0.10 to overall\n    89→\n    90→**Recommended priority:** Fix Issues #1-3 together (narrator profile generation) as they're related. This would:\n    91→- Improve Character Profiles from 5 to ~7 (+0.30 overall)\n    92→- Potentially improve Character Extraction slightly (+0.05-0.10 overall)\n    93→- Total expected gain: ~0.35-0.40 points, crossing the 8.0 threshold\n    94→\n    95→## Fix History\n    96→\n    97→### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic\n    98→- Removed overly aggressive auto-acceptance of high-mention-count names\n    99→- Enhanced validation system prompt to reject objects/food/drink\n   100→- Result: Amontillado no longer extracted, narrator correctly identified in plot_summary\n   101→\n   102→### Attempt 2 (2026-01-18): Fix